# autotune-found: the fine-tuning assistant (issue #100) finding a better spot.
# Same trigger as `autotune` (page APP 6, "Auto Tune" button -> the scan runs),
# but this fixture pushes a synthetic S-meter with a peak 1500 Hz below the dial
# (src/screens.c, autotune_found_slice; the bank has no DSP to update the real
# S-meter). The scan measures every probe and leaves the dial on the peak:
# 14.072.500. This is the "spot picked up" path, with the same algorithm that
# runs on the radio; the real "which spot sounds better" correlation is the
# owner's radio (docs/autotune.md).

name autotune-found
screen autotune-found

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
